      "writtenOn": "2025-10-17T21:35:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried this inside the loop like suggested:\n\n{% set callbackInfo_member \u003d find_by_name(by_category[\"callback info\"], member.name.get() ~ \" info\") %}\n{% if callbackInfo_member and find_by_name(callbackInfo_member.members, \u0027mode\u0027) %}\n       callbackInfo.mode \u003d WGPUCallbackMode_AllowSpontaneous;\n{% endif %}\n\n\nThe problem is that by_category[\"callback info\"] contains full names (e.g., \u0027request device callback info\u0027, \u0027device lost callback info\u0027..), but member.name.get() sometimes only provides a partial name (e.g., \u0027callback\u0027, \u0027device lost callback\u0027 respectively).\n\nFor callbacks with similar patterns, like \u0027device lost callback\u0027, the logic find_by_name(by_category[\"callback info\"], member.name.get() ~ \" info\") works because it correctly finds \u0027device lost callback info\u0027 member.\n\nHowever, for a \u0027request device callback\u0027, the member name is just \u0027callback\u0027, so my code is looking for \u0027callback info\u0027, which isn\u0027t able to find the corresponding \u0027request device callback info\u0027 member.\n\nTLDR: The member.name is not consistent with the callback info names. I see this CL has been merged. I can try to address this later if I\u0027m able to find a way of doing this.",
      "parentUuid": "3e681ebc_8f0955a4",
